void reverse(Node* head) {
    Node* prev = NULL;
    Node* curr = head;
    while (curr != NULL) {
        Node* next = curr->next;
        curr->next = prev;
        prev = curr;
        curr = next;
    }
}
```

This function takes the head of the linked list as input and reverses it. It uses two pointers to traverse the list, one for the previous node and another for the current node. The `prev` pointer keeps track of the last node we visited, and the `next` pointer points to the new first node after the reversed part.
